 "text": "You didn't quit your goal, you just stopped seeing it. Why do we stop doing things we know are good for us? Reason 16. Week 1 you think about it every day, by week 3 only when someone asks how it's going. Nothing in your day points at it, it lives in a notes app you never open. So put it where your eyes already go, your lock screen the goal in this week's one step. Now you see it every time you pick up your phone. And every Sunday two minutes, cross off this week's step and write the next one. Goal on the lock screen one step two minutes on Sunday. Send this to the friend whose goal lives in a notes app. That's what D-Mure is for. Archive your dream today and break it into small steps you can actually do. Follow for one reason a day. Next, why two hours on Sunday is the slowest way to learn. Where does your goal live right now? The link's in the bio.",
